@style(../styles/IDocDemo.style)
@title(Accessibility and audio)

Read aloud, spoken maths, Braille and audio players.

@section(Accessibility)

@subsection(@@enable)

Turn on document features — notably accessibility, which adds per-equation listen buttons and a whole-document Read aloud.

@enable(accessibility)

@subsection(@@say)

Speak text with the neural voice — math inside $…$ is read as English.

@say(Welcome to lecture 1)

@say(text=…, voice=mika, rate=1.1)

@say(eq=med.Beer-Lambert-Intensity)

@say(eq=med.bl, expanded)

@say(text=The circuit has two resistors., speak=The circuit has two resistors in series., pitch=1, energy=1.1, articulation=crisp, autoplay)

@say(text=This line is read with the neutral voice., emotion=neutral)

@say(text=This line is read with the calm voice., emotion=calm)

@say(text=This line is read with the confident voice., emotion=confident)

@say(text=This line is read with the warm voice., emotion=warm)

@say(text=This line is read with the sad voice., emotion=sad)

@say(text=This line is read with the angry voice., emotion=angry)

@say(text=This line is read with the fearful voice., emotion=fearful)

@say(text=This line is read with the excited voice., emotion=excited)

@say(text=This line is read with the reassuring voice., emotion=reassuring)

@say(text=This line is read with the urgent voice., emotion=urgent)

@say(text=This line uses the default context., context=default)

@say(text=This line uses the formal context., context=formal)

@say(text=This line uses the conversational context., context=conversational)

@say(text=This line uses the clinical context., context=clinical)

@say(text=This line uses the educational context., context=educational)

@subsection(@@braille)

Render text as Braille — and, at the top of a document, export the whole thing as a 3-D printable Braille plate.

@braille(Hello)

@braille()

@braille(eq=med.bl)

@section(Audio)

@subsection(@@audioplayer)

An audio player — one file, or dir=folder for a playlist.

@audioplayer(file=tone-a.wav)

@audioplayer(dir=lecture1)

One file, with a name for @@ref, looping: @audioplayer(src=tone-a.wav, label=A 440 Hz tone, loop)

A playlist of two files: @audioplayer(tracks="tone-a.wav, tone-d.wav", label=Two tones)

Starts on load: @audioplayer(src=tone-d.wav, autoplay)

@@audio is the same as @@audioplayer: @audio(src=tone-a.wav, label=Tone)
